## Proposal

* Decouple all DAG execution and resolution logic from MLMD.
* Expose all formerly-MLMD data via the KFP API server, enabling the KFP UI to consume this data through the API server rather than MLMD.
* Ensure the transition from MLMD to the new API has minimal impact on the UI:
    * Retain support for the "Artifacts" navigation tab.
    * Remove the "Executions" tab, which is not meaningful post-MLMD.
      * Any relevant information can be surfaced in the component details section
* Ensure compatibility and feature completeness by analyzing MLMD proto definitions and comparing API coverage.
* Store the following domain entities directly in the KFP database:
    * Artifact metadata
    * Metrics
    * Inputs/Outputs parameters
* There should be a migration strategy for users moving to a release with no MLMD:
    * Users must run a one-time migration script to move MLMD data into the KFP database.
    * The KFP API server should fail to start if the migration has not been completed.
